
# architecture-site-design.skill.md

Skill: Architecture Site Design

Description:
- Principles and best practices for designing architecture-focused websites: layout, typography, imagery, portfolio presentation, and accessibility.

Key Competencies:
- Responsive grid and layout techniques for showcasing projects.
- High-quality image optimization and lazy-loading strategies.
- Minimal, elegant typography and visual hierarchy for architectural content.
- Interactive project galleries and case-study templates.
- Performance optimization and accessibility (ARIA, semantic HTML).

Usage Examples:
- Create a portfolio landing page with a masonry or CSS grid of project cards.
- Build project detail pages with full-bleed hero images, project metadata, and descriptive sections.
- Implement filterable galleries (by typology, year, scale) with accessible controls.

Notes:
- Focus on clean visuals, large imagery, and clear navigation for professionals and clients.
- Prioritize performance and mobile-first responsive design.
